<title>CHINA: China signs $130 mln order for CFM jet engines.</title>
<headline>China signs $130 mln order for CFM jet engines.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>China has signed an agreement to buy passenger jet engines from CFM International in a deal worth $130 million, the official Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>CFM International is a joint venture between General Electric Co of the United States and Snecma of France.  </p>
<p>The CFM56-5B4 engines would be used on 13 A320 passenger jets already on order from Airbus Industrie, Xinhua said in a report issued late on Monday.</p>
<p>The aircraft would be put into service by two domestic carriers, China Northwest Airlines and Zhejiang Airlines, over the next four years, Xinhua said quoting official sources.</p>
<p>The new agency said that the accord was signed on Monday ahead of an international air show in Zhuhai in south China.</p>
</text>
